        "message": "fix(68): the iOS archive check globbed the wrong directory — everything built fine\n\nRun 36687275393, job 109795907926:\n\n    ::error::build-arm64 has 0 archive(s); llama needs llama, ggml, ggml-cpu\n             and ggml-base at minimum.\n\nNOT A BUILD FAILURE. Every archive was produced in that run:\n\n    [35/209] Linking CXX static library ggml/src/ggml-metal/libggml-metal.a\n    [39/209] Linking CXX static library ggml/src/libggml-cpu.a\n    [40/209] Linking CXX static library ggml/src/libggml.a\n    [209/209] Linking CXX static library src/libllama.a\n\nand the step's own listing says exactly where they are:\n\n    === archives for arm64 ===\n    build-arm64/ggml/src/ggml-blas/libggml-blas.a\n    build-arm64/ggml/src/ggml-metal/libggml-metal.a\n    build-arm64/ggml/src/libggml-base.a\n    build-arm64/ggml/src/libggml-cpu.a\n    build-arm64/ggml/src/libggml.a\n    build-arm64/src/libllama.a\n\nA CMAKE BUILD WRITES EACH ARCHIVE NEXT TO ITS SOURCE, not into one output\ndirectory. So `\"$DIR\"/*.a` matched none of them, and a check looking in the\nwrong place reported a build that had just succeeded as one that had not.\n\nThis is the second time in this repository, and android-deps already records the\nlesson:\n\n    # A cmake build writes archives next to their sources, so find them\n    # anywhere and print every .a when there is none. A verify step that\n    # asserts a hardcoded path is a guess.\n\nSo `find -name '*.a'`, and each required archive is required BY NAME:\n\n    for NAME in llama ggml ggml-cpu ggml-base; do\n      A=$(echo \"$MAP\" | grep -E \"/lib$NAME\\.a$\" | sed -n '1p')\n      [ -n \"$A\" ] || { echo \"::error::$DIR has no lib$NAME.a\"; exit 1; }\n\nBY NAME, NOT BY COUNT. The old check was `-lt 4`, which four copies of one\nlibrary satisfy while nothing links. Both failure modes tested against a fixture\nlaid out like the real one:\n\n    glob fakebuild/*.a        -> 0 archives      <- the bug\n    find fakebuild -name *.a  -> all 5 found\n    by name: libllama.a, libggml.a, libggml-cpu.a, libggml-base.a   all found\n    4 files named liba/libb/libc/libd, no libllama.a\n                              -> correctly rejected, where a count would pass\n\nTHE PACKAGING STEP HAD THE SAME ASSUMPTION and would have copied zero archives\ninto every package, producing a prebuilt tree with no lib/ contents and a\nfailure much later in cargo that names neither the job nor the cause. It now\nuses find as well, and refuses to finish with fewer than four archives.\n\nWhen a directory has no archives at all, the step prints its first 20\nsubdirectories, so the next reader sees the actual layout rather than only\n\"0 archives\".\nMSG",
